# Databricks notebook source
"""
Silver table reconciliation:  core (read replica)  vs  core_tst_std001 (CDA)
=============================================================================

INPUTS (notebook widgets, or key=value job arguments)
  table_names      one or more schema.table, separated by comma / semicolon / new line.
                   Optional per-table key:  schema.table:key1|key2
                     e.g.  silver.customer:customer_id, silver.orders:order_id|line_no, silver.product
  key_columns      default business key for tables without their own key (optional, comma-separated)
  exclude_columns  extra columns to ignore. LOAD_DT and HASH_DIFF are ALWAYS excluded.
  filter_column    window column, default SYS_EFCTV_DT
  filter_start     window start (inclusive):  'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss' | 'yyyy-MM-dd' | DAILY | blank
  filter_end       window end   (exclusive):  same formats
                   DAILY in either field = yesterday 05:00 -> today 05:00.
                   Both blank = whole data compared.
                   Filter column missing in either table = whole data compared on BOTH sides.
  sample_rows      sample unmatched records stored per table (default 20)

CHECKS (one scan per side, only SHA-256 row hashes are cached -> suits large daily full refresh)
  EXISTENCE  both tables readable
  SCHEMA     columns added/removed on either side (comparison continues on the common columns,
             possible renames flagged), data type, nullability, name case, column order
  FILTER     SYS_EFCTV_DT window applied or reason it was not
  COUNT      row counts
  DATA       full-record compare of every row on all common columns, strict and format-normalised
             (whitespace, blank vs NULL, numeric scale, date/timestamp format, string<->typed cast)
             incl. "all records matched but one side has extra rows" and duplicate records
  FORMAT     per-column format differences
  KEY        (when key given) missing keys each side, duplicate keys, per-column value mismatches
  PROFILE    per-column NULL / blank counts
  Every step is isolated: a failing step is logged as ERROR and the remaining steps still run;
  a failing table does not stop the other tables.

OUTPUT  (core_tst_std001.testing_sb, Delta, appended every run, created / extended automatically)
  recon_summary           one row per table per run
  recon_check_results     one row per finding, detailed comments
  recon_mismatch_samples  full sample records that did not match
  recon_summary_latest    view: latest run per table per day
  latest_run_ind = 'Y' only on the latest run of a table for each run_date; earlier runs that day -> 'N'
"""

